libarch descends only into amd64: the other architectures' directories are not in the tree.

The trees keep only the Kernel's architectures, arm64 and amd64 (the user's decision of
2026-11-08); tools/layout.py does not copy alpha, arm, i386 and mips64 here. arm64 has no
directory of its own in libarch.

--- a/Makefile
+++ b/Makefile
@@ -1,6 +1,6 @@
 #	$OpenBSD: Makefile,v 1.8 2009/09/27 18:20:11 miod Exp $
 #	$NetBSD: Makefile,v 1.8 1996/02/21 02:43:52 jtk Exp $
 
-SUBDIR=	alpha amd64 arm i386 mips64
+SUBDIR=	amd64
 
 .include <bsd.subdir.mk>
